Thanks to Dr. Thomas Blinn (thomas.blinn@hp.com) and
Jeffrey Hummel (Jeffrey_Hummel@albemarle.com) for the help.

So, the value of the parameter LOADADDR of the Kernel configuration file is
hardware dependent.
To get the right value for your hardware:
- generate the configuration file with 'sizer -n <config_file_name>'
command,
- examine the generated '/tmp/<config_file_name>' to get the value of
LOADADDR parameter.

Regards,
Alex Zakoshanski
alexander.zakoshanski@alcatel.com.au


The original question was:

>
> Hi All,
>
> Could you please tell me what are the rules for setting of values for
> LOADADDR in the Kernel configuration files /sys/conf/<HOSTNAME> on Tru64
> Unix v5.1?
>
> Re:
>
> # diff HOSTA HOSTB
> 81c81
> < makeoptions   LOADADDR="fffffc0000830000"
> ---
> > makeoptions   LOADADDR="fffffc0000430000"
>
>
> Thanks and Regards,
> Alex Zakoshanski
> alexander.zakoshanski@alcatel.com.au



